# Python Imports

## Never use `__all__`

Do not define `__all__` in any module. Import from the defining module instead of re-exporting through package barrels.

```python
# ❌ BAD
__all__ = []
__all__ = ["Settings", "get_settings"]

# ✅ GOOD
from app.config.settings import Settings, get_settings
```

## Use full imports from defining modules

Import symbols from the module where they are defined. Do not rely on package `__init__.py` re-exports or wildcard imports.

```python
# ❌ BAD
from app.config import get_settings
from app.db.models import Base
from app.config.settings import *

# ✅ GOOD
from app.config.settings import get_settings
from app.db.base import Base
```

When adding or updating imports, trace the symbol to its source module and import from there.
